// `vcode`: what every target of the Grasm backend shares below instruction
// selection (docs/self-hosting.md §6.16).
//
//     target.gr    the target description each instruction set fills in
//     vcode.gr     machine instructions over virtual registers
//     regalloc.gr  linear-scan allocation, for fast builds, and the spill
//                  rewrite both allocators end in
//     backtrack.gr the release allocator: backtracking by spill weight
//     check.gr     the symbolic checker every allocation must pass
//     frameplan.gr where the frame is set up (shrink-wrapping)
//     moves.gr     moves, and block arguments as parallel moves
//
// Nothing here names a register or an opcode of any instruction set: each
// target (`compiler/aarch64`, `compiler/x86_64`) describes itself in a
// `Target` and selects, encodes and lays out frames itself.
import target
import vcode
import regalloc
import backtrack
import check
import frameplan
import moves
